Day 03 of my bug bounty series: setting up the environment.

Before hunting anything, I wanted my setup to be clean. A messy setup wastes hours.

Today I set up 4 things:

1. Burp Suite: it sits between my browser and the website, so I can see every request.
2. Browser setup: Firefox now sends its traffic through Burp's proxy.
3. Extensions: Wappalyzer shows the tech behind a site. Cookie Editor lets me read and edit cookies.
4. Workspace: one folder and one notes app for everything. If it's not written down, it didn't happen.

Tools don't find bugs. But a good setup makes it easier to notice them.

